# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Backlog

> **Track**: {{PROJECT_NAME}} (`{{AGENT_PREFIX}}-`)
> **What this file is**: the **hot working set** — only items that are still
> `open` or `wip`. It is NOT the archive of all work ever. Done-ness is *derived*,
> not asserted here: an item is done iff it has left this file and appears in
> [`archive/backlog-archive.md`](./archive/backlog-archive.md) (the cold ledger,
> grepped on demand) pointing at the sprint that closed it — cross-checkable
> against that sprint's board.
> **Delivery record**: the active sprint's board (`sprints/S<N>/tasks.md`) owns
> in-flight task state; the cold archive owns closed items.
> **Discipline**: keep `## Active` **open/wip-only**. The moment a row reaches a
> terminal status it is swept out — never edit a row into a done-narrative.
> Status is **one token, never a log** (see the enum below).
> **Last updated**: YYYY-MM-DD
> **Next ID**: B001 · **Next follow-up**: F0001

Backlog row format + the status enum → [`../designs/_templates/BACKLOG_ENTRY_TEMPLATE.md`](../designs/_templates/BACKLOG_ENTRY_TEMPLATE.md).
Hygiene is mechanical: `scripts/backlog.sh check | sweep | verify <ID>` (0 LLM
tokens) + a CI gate. Rationale → [`../setup/index-discipline.md`](../setup/index-discipline.md).

## Complexity Scale

| Size | Estimate | Example |
|------|----------|---------|
| S | ~1 task group | Seed data, simple config |
| M | ~2-3 task groups | CRUD backend or frontend |
| L | ~4-6 task groups | Full feature (backend + frontend + tests) |
| XL | ~7+ task groups | Complex feature (real-time, multi-repo, etc.) |

